│ patch_description        │ This version switches from a long-horizon indicator stack to a regime-normalized,         │
│                          │ short-memory feature model. The core idea is to make each input more stationary across    │
│                          │ market shifts by using rolling z-scores, rank transforms, and short-window rate-of-change │
│                          │ features instead of raw absolute levels.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Compared with the current implementation, this approach:                                  │
│                          │ - emphasizes 5–20 bar dynamics that decay faster but are more regime-robust,              │
│                          │ - normalizes price/volume/volatility features within rolling windows to reduce regime     │
│                          │ dependence,                                                                               │
│                          │ - adds explicit “change of market character” features like volatility trend, efficiency   │
│                          │ trend, and autocorrelation trend,                                                         │
│                          │ - uses compact interaction terms such as momentum × volatility regime,                    │
│                          │ - regularizes XGBoost more heavily and reduces model complexity to discourage memorizing  │
│                          │ train-only regimes.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result should be less prediction collapse on validation, with better slope            │
│                          │ preservation and improved generalization across the second regime shift.                  │
