│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the strongest ideas from both prior implementations while explicitly │
│                          │ targeting the train→val regime collapse.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Shorter, more regime-robust lookbacks dominate the feature set.                         │
│                          │ - Rolling z-score / normalized features are added to make features less scale-dependent   │
│                          │ across volatility regimes.                                                                │
│                          │ - New “rate of change of market character” features capture changes in volatility,        │
│                          │ efficiency, and autocorrelation instead of only absolute levels.                          │
│                          │ - Momentum × volatility-regime interactions are preserved, but simplified and made more   │
│                          │ robust.                                                                                   │
│                          │ - XGBoost is regularized more carefully than the current overfit-heavy version: shallower │
│                          │ trees, higher min_child_weight, moderate subsampling, and stronger regularization.        │
│                          │ - Feature count remains comfortably below 80 and all features use only past data.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation is still compatible with the same interface and return format, and it  │
│                          │ avoids changing anything outside the EVOLVE blocks and constants. It should be more       │
│                          │ stable on the validation regime while preserving enough expressivity to avoid collapsing  │
│                          │ predictions toward the mean.                                                              │
