│ patch_description        │ This edit aims to reduce regime-specific overfitting by shifting the feature set away     │
│                          │ from long-horizon absolute levels and toward short-horizon, rolling standardized signals. │
│                          │ The main idea is:                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Replace the broad set of long lookbacks with shorter, more responsive windows.          │
│                          │ - Add rolling z-score normalization for returns, volatility, and volume so the model sees │
│                          │ regime-invariant deviations instead of raw magnitudes.                                    │
│                          │ - Add “market character change” features such as volatility trend, efficiency trend, and  │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend.                                                                    │
│                          │ - Keep the important momentum × volatility interaction, but make it more robust via       │
│                          │ short-window inputs.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Reduce model capacity slightly and add regularization to force the booster to focus on  │
│                          │ stable patterns and improve validation slope.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help the model preserve slope on the validation regime while also increasing  │
│                          │ prediction dispersion away from the current near-mean collapse.                           │
