│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode: the model’s slope collapses in the validation    │
│                          │ regime because the current feature set is dominated by absolute, long-horizon signals     │
│                          │ that do not survive regime shifts. I propose two coordinated changes:                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Make the booster less prone to fitting brittle, high-variance patterns by reducing     │
│                          │ depth/estimators and adding modest regularization.                                        │
│                          │ 2. Rebuild features around short lookbacks, rolling z-scores, and change-of-regime        │
│                          │ signals. This emphasizes rate-of-change and normalized structure rather than absolute     │
│                          │ levels, which should improve cross-regime transfer and lift validation slope without      │
│                          │ inflating feature count.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The resulting feature set stays compact, uses only past data, and keeps all interactions  │
│                          │ causal.                                                                                   │
