│ patch_name               │ regime_shortlook_xgb                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover version keeps the stable parts of the prior implementations while shifting │
│                          │ feature design toward shorter, more regime-invariant windows. The main changes are:       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - shorter lookbacks focused on 5–20 bars, with only a few 40-bar context features         │
│                          │ - rolling z-score normalization for returns, volume, range, and momentum features         │
│                          │ - explicit features for regime change rather than only absolute regime levels             │
│                          │ - a momentum × volatility-regime interaction retained as a compact, high-signal feature   │
│                          │ - slightly more conservative XGBoost settings to reduce overfitting and improve val slope │
│                          │ stability                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to preserve directional information while reducing dependence on              │
│                          │ train-specific market regimes, which should help the model generalize better into the     │
│                          │ validation period without increasing feature count beyond the limit.                      │
