│ patch_description        │ This version crosses the broader feature set from the earlier implementations with the    │
│                          │ stronger normalization and regime-shift focus from the current program.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main changes:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Shorter lookbacks dominate the feature set, which should help the model adapt faster to │
│                          │ the second regime shift.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Rolling z-scores are used more aggressively to make features regime-invariant.          │
│                          │ - Added “change in market character” features: volatility trend, autocorrelation trend,   │
│                          │ efficiency trend, and dispersion trend.                                                   │
│                          │ - Kept a few robust longer-window anchors, but reduced their dominance.                   │
│                          │ - Added momentum × volatility-regime interactions in a more compact and normalized form.  │
│                          │ - Relaxed the current heavy regularization to reduce prediction collapse while still      │
│                          │ keeping overfit controlled.                                                               │
│                          │ - Feature count stays safely below 80.                                                    │
