│ patch_description        │ This edit focuses on the root failure mode: the model’s slope collapses in the newest     │
│                          │ regime and predictions are too mean-reverting. I’m making the feature space more          │
│                          │ regime-invariant by emphasizing short windows and rolling z-normalized transforms, while  │
│                          │ also adding explicit “change in market character” features such as volatility trend,      │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend, and efficiency trend. These are more likely to survive a second    │
│                          │ regime shift than absolute levels.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the model side, I slightly increase expressivity by reducing regularization and tree   │
│                          │ constraints a bit, while keeping the ensemble size moderate to avoid overfitting. The     │
│                          │ goal is to raise pred_std_ratio and val slope without losing the current acceptable       │
│                          │ directional accuracy. The feature count remains safely below 80.                          │
