│ patch_description        │ This crossover version combines the strongest parts of the prior implementations while    │
│                          │ emphasizing the main failure mode: regime collapse on the validation period. The feature  │
│                          │ set is rebuilt around shorter lookbacks, rolling z-scores, volatility/trend-change        │
│                          │ signals, and a few robust multiplicative interactions such as momentum × volatility       │
│                          │ regime. I also keep the feature count comfortably below the 80-feature limit and preserve │
│                          │ the exact input/output interface.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the model side, the hyperparameters are adjusted to be slightly less regularized and a │
│                          │ bit more expressive than the current program, while still using moderate tree depth and   │
│                          │ early stopping to avoid runaway overfit. The goal is to improve validation slope and      │
│                          │ correlation without sacrificing directional accuracy.                                     │
