│ patch_description        │ This crossover version blends the stronger parts of the prior implementations while       │
│                          │ targeting the main failure mode: regime-specific features that lose slope on the          │
│                          │ validation period.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Shifts feature emphasis toward shorter lookbacks and faster-decaying market structure.  │
│                          │ - Adds rolling z-score / normalized versions of momentum, volatility, volume, and range   │
│                          │ features to make them more regime-invariant.                                              │
│                          │ - Includes explicit regime-change features such as volatility trend, autocorrelation      │
│                          │ trend, and efficiency trend.                                                              │
│                          │ - Keeps the feature count safely below 80 while preserving the strongest robust signals.  │
│                          │ - Uses a slightly less collapsed XGBoost configuration: moderate depth, lower             │
│                          │ regularization than the most constrained versions, and enough estimators for expressivity │
│                          │ without overfitting too hard.                                                             │
│                          │ - Preserves the original program interface and behavior outside the evolved blocks.       │
