│ patch_name               │ adaptive_expressivity_boost                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current model is severely over-regularized, causing predictions to collapse toward    │
│                          │ the mean (pred_std_ratio=0.035, train_slope=0.0076). The primary issue is excessive       │
│                          │ regularization combined with insufficient model capacity.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of the problem:                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. The model has max_depth=3, min_child_weight=10, reg_lambda=8.0, reg_alpha=1.5, and     │
│                          │ gamma=0.2 - all extremely conservative                                                    │
│                          │ 2. This heavy regularization is destroying the model's ability to learn even the training │
│                          │ patterns                                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. The slope collapse (val_slope=0.0016, train_slope=0.0076) indicates the model cannot   │
│                          │ express directional predictions                                                           │
│                          │ 4. The good news: generalization_ratio=85.4% means what little the model learns does      │
│                          │ generalize well                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Significantly increase model expressivity by reducing regularization and increasing    │
│                          │ depth                                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. Add more estimators but with a higher learning rate to maintain training speed         │
│                          │ 3. Keep min_child_weight moderate to preserve some generalization                         │
│                          │ 4. The features are already well-designed with z-score normalization and short lookbacks, │
│                          │ so we mainly need to let the model use them                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Train slope should increase from 0.0076 to at least 0.020 (3x improvement)              │
│                          │ - Pred_std_ratio should increase from 0.035 to at least 0.10 (3x improvement)             │
│                          │ - With the strong feature engineering already in place, the generalization ratio should   │
│                          │ remain good (>60%)                                                                        │
│                          │ - Target: val_slope >= 0.020, val_DA >= 0.520                                             │
