│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the two main failure modes: prediction collapse and regime fragility. I │
│                          │ reduce over-regularization slightly so XGBoost can express more slope, while keeping      │
│                          │ depth moderate to avoid overfit. On the feature side, I add more regime-invariant         │
│                          │ short-horizon signals: rolling z-scored volatility, rolling z-scored trend, and a compact │
│                          │ volatility-adjusted momentum interaction. These are designed to survive the               │
│                          │ train→test→val regime shift better than absolute-level indicators. The new features are   │
│                          │ all causal and keep the total feature count safely below the 80-feature limit.            │
