│ patch_description        │ This crossover version keeps the stronger short-horizon and regime-aware ideas from the   │
│                          │ better prior programs, while reducing dependence on long lookbacks that appeared to       │
│                          │ overfit the earlier regime.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Uses shorter rolling windows more heavily (5/10/20/40) to improve regime adaptability.  │
│                          │ - Adds rolling z-scored returns and z-scored volume to normalize across changing          │
│                          │ volatility environments.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Adds explicit “market character change” features: volatility trend, efficiency trend,   │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend, and regime-change deltas.                                          │
│                          │ - Keeps a compact feature count under the 80-feature limit while preserving the most      │
│                          │ useful price, volatility, momentum, range, volume, and interaction signals.               │
│                          │ - Uses a slightly less constrained XGBoost setup than the collapsing version, but still   │
│                          │ regularized enough to avoid extreme overfit.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The interface, inputs, outputs, and run_experiment logic remain unchanged.                │
