│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_conditional_features                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current best program achieves 96.0% generalization ratio but suffers from a val_slope │
│                          │ that's only 7.8% of train_slope. The key insight from the best performer is that it       │
│                          │ includes `vol_regime_rank` and `vol_regime_20_40` but doesn't use them to modulate other  │
│                          │ features adaptively.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I will implement regime-conditional versions of the top-performing features by creating   │
│                          │ multiplicative interactions between momentum, efficiency, and autocorrelation features    │
│                          │ with volatility regime indicators. This approach makes features explicitly adapt to       │
│                          │ market conditions rather than assuming static relationships.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Specifically, I will:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Create high-volatility versions of momentum features (ret_3, ret_5) by multiplying     │
│                          │ with (vol_regime_rank > 0.7)                                                              │
│                          │ 2. Create low-volatility versions of efficiency and autocorrelation features by           │
│                          │ multiplying with (vol_regime_rank < 0.3)                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Add regime-conditional RSI features that behave differently in different volatility    │
│                          │ environments                                                                              │
│                          │ 4. Create a volatility regime transition indicator to capture regime shifts               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve the slope ratio by making the model learn regime-specific patterns    │
│                          │ that generalize better across the train→test→val boundaries.                              │
