│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ short_regime_xgb                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current model uses deep, heavily cross-regime features with a very strong predictive  │
│                          │ collapse toward the mean on validation. Its key parameters are `n_estimators=400`,        │
│                          │ `max_depth=5`, `min_child_weight=1`, and effectively no regularization (`reg_alpha=0`,    │
│                          │ `reg_lambda=0`), which encourages the model to overfit train-specific structure while     │
│                          │ still under-producing variance out of sample.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This rewrite shifts the bias toward shorter, regime-invariant features and less brittle   │
│                          │ tree learning:                                                                            │
│                          │ - shorter lookbacks for returns, volatility, trend, and oscillators                       │
│                          │ - rolling z-score / rank transforms to normalize feature scale across regimes             │
│                          │ - explicit regime-change features such as volatility trend, efficiency trend, and         │
│                          │ autocorrelation proxies                                                                   │
│                          │ - a compact momentum × volatility interaction to preserve useful nonlinear structure      │
│                          │ - slightly stronger but not excessive tree constraints to reduce collapse while keeping   │
│                          │ enough expressivity:                                                                      │
│                          │   - lower depth than the current program                                                  │
│                          │   - moderate `min_child_weight`                                                           │
│                          │   - small L1/L2 regularization instead of none                                            │
│                          │   - more trees with smaller learning rate for smoother fit                                │
│                          │ - slightly less aggressive target clipping to retain slope                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help raise validation slope and prediction variance while improving           │
│                          │ robustness across the second regime shift.                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
