│ patch_name               │ regime_shift_xgb                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover version keeps the strongest parts of the prior implementations while       │
│                          │ focusing on the main failure mode: regime-specific predictions that collapse on           │
│                          │ validation. I combined shorter lookbacks, rolling z-score normalization, volatility/trend │
│                          │ change features, and a compact set of interaction terms that are more likely to           │
│                          │ generalize across the train→test→val regime shifts.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Uses shorter, regime-invariant feature windows more aggressively.                       │
│                          │ - Adds explicit “change in market character” signals: volatility trend, efficiency trend, │
│                          │ trend acceleration, and rank/z-score transforms.                                          │
│                          │ - Keeps feature count compact to avoid overfitting and satisfy runtime constraints.       │
│                          │ - Slightly increases model expressivity while preventing collapse with moderate           │
│                          │ regularization and smaller child weights than the current baseline.                       │
│                          │ - Preserves the exact interface and output format.                                        │
