                        Patch Metadata - Gen 45/150 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ regime_shortlook_xgb                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the strongest robust ideas from both families of programs while      │
│                          │ targeting the main failure mode: validation slope collapse under regime shift.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Uses shorter lookbacks more aggressively (5–20 bars) to favor faster-decaying signals   │
│                          │ that are more likely to survive the train→test→val shift.                                 │
│                          │ - Adds rolling z-score normalization for several core signals so the model sees           │
│                          │ regime-invariant versions of momentum, volatility, and volume.                            │
│                          │ - Emphasizes “change in market character” features: volatility trend, efficiency trend,   │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend, dispersion trend, and short/long regime deltas.                    │
