╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ short_regime_boost                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This edit attacks the two dominant failure modes in the current model: prediction         │
│                          │ collapse and regime fragility.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Hyperparameters:                                                                       │
│                          │    - Increase learning rate modestly and reduce excessive L1/L2 + child weight            │
│                          │ regularization so trees can express more signal.                                          │
│                          │    - Keep depth shallow to avoid overfit, but raise subsampling slightly and reduce       │
│                          │ `min_child_weight` so the model can use more splits.                                      │
│                          │    - Lower `early_stopping_rounds` a bit to match the higher learning rate.               │
│                          │    - Slightly relax target clipping to preserve more tail information, which helps        │
│                          │ slope/variance.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Features:                                                                              │
│                          │    - Replace longer-horizon, regime-specific signals with shorter lookback versions where │
│                          │ possible.                                                                                 │
│                          │    - Add rolling z-score normalization for price, return, volume, and volatility so the   │
│                          │ model sees regime-invariant inputs.                                                       │
│                          │    - Add explicit change-in-market-character features: volatility trend, autocorr trend,  │
│                          │ efficiency trend, dispersion trend.                                                       │
│                          │    - Add a compact momentum × volatility-regime interaction, which often generalizes      │
│                          │ better than the raw components alone.                                                     │
│                          │    - Keep feature count safely under 80 by pruning a few weaker long-horizon features.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes should improve val slope and pred_std_ratio while preserving the already    │
│                          │ decent DA. The goal is to make the model less “mean-collapsed” and less dependent on one  │
│                          │ regime.                                                                                   │
