│ patch_description        │ This crossover version keeps the stronger parts of both prior implementations while       │
│                          │ pushing harder toward regime invariance and shorter-horizon signals.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main changes:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Uses shorter lookbacks for momentum, volatility, mean reversion, and regime features.   │
│                          │ - Adds rolling z-scores and rank-based transforms to reduce regime dependence.            │
│                          │ - Emphasizes “change in market character” features such as volatility trend, trend        │
│                          │ change, efficiency change, and regime shifts.                                             │
│                          │ - Keeps only robust multiplicative interactions like momentum × volatility regime and     │
│                          │ volume × price pressure.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Reduces model over-complexity slightly versus the current program to improve            │
│                          │ generalization across the second regime shift.                                            │
│                          │ - Maintains the same inputs, outputs, and interface, and stays within the feature-count   │
│                          │ and runtime constraints.                                                                  │
