│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_adaptive_short_horizon                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This edit focuses on the main failure mode: the model still learns brittle,               │
│                          │ regime-specific relationships that vanish in validation. I’m tightening the tree ensemble │
│                          │ to reduce train-overfit while adding explicitly regime-conditioned versions of the        │
│                          │ strongest short-horizon signals.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The feature changes do three things:                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Add short lookback, rolling-z normalized variants of return and price-location         │
│                          │ features, which are more stable across volatility regimes.                                │
│                          │ 2. Add regime-adaptive interactions that modulate momentum and efficiency by current      │
│                          │ volatility regime, making the same signal mean different things in high- vs low-vol       │
│                          │ markets.                                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Add rate-of-change features for regime character itself, so the model can react to     │
│                          │ shifts rather than absolute levels.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hyperparameter changes reduce depth and model size a bit, and increase child weight / │
│                          │ regularization, which should help preserve slope on validation by discouraging overly     │
│                          │ specific splits. I also slightly relax target clipping to keep more usable signal         │
│                          │ amplitude, since the current model is already collapsing toward the mean.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All changes stay within the feature-count limit and use only past data.                   │
