│ patch_description        │ The current program is severely over-regularized, causing predictions to collapse toward  │
│                          │ the mean (slope_ratio=20.7%, pred_std_ratio=3.5%). I'm reducing regularization parameters │
│                          │ and increasing model capacity to allow learning transferable patterns. Additionally, I'm  │
│                          │ extending the multi-scale z-score normalization approach from the best prior program      │
│                          │ (which achieved 96% generalization) by adding ret_z features at windows [10, 20, 40, 60]  │
│                          │ and creating explicit regime shift indicators (ret_z_20 - ret_z_60, ret_z_40 - ret_z_60)  │
│                          │ that signal when recent behavior diverges from longer-term patterns. These regime shift   │
│                          │ indicators are key for handling the train→test→val regime transitions. I'm removing the   │
│                          │ less predictive time-of-day features (hour_sin, hour_cos, dow_sin, dow_cos) to stay under │
│                          │ 80 features.                                                                              │
