│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ short_regime_shift                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode directly: the model has decent train/test signal  │
│                          │ but the slope collapses on the most recent regime. I’m making two coordinated changes.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Hyperparameters: slightly reduce regularization and tree fragmentation while keeping   │
│                          │ enough constraints to avoid overfitting. The current model is too expressive in a         │
│                          │ regime-specific way, but also underpowered in the latest regime because it collapses      │
│                          │ toward the mean. A modestly lower learning rate, fewer trees than the current 400, lower  │
│                          │ min_child_weight, and a touch more subsampling should improve usable expressivity without │
│                          │ letting the model memorize train-only structure. Reducing early stopping a bit keeps      │
│                          │ training focused on the strongest trees.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Features: replace long-horizon, regime-fragile signals with shorter windows and        │
│                          │ explicit regime-change features. The update emphasizes 5–20 bar windows, rolling          │
│                          │ z-scores, and differences between short and medium horizons so the model can react to     │
│                          │ changes in market character rather than absolute levels. I also add a direct momentum ×   │
│                          │ volatility-regime interaction and keep the feature count safely under 80.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help raise val slope and pred_std_ratio while improving regime robustness     │
│                          │ across the test→val shift.                                                                │
