                        Patch Metadata - Gen 51/150 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_percentile_rank_features_for_distribution_invariance                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program shows strong train performance (train_slope=0.0738) but severe        │
│                          │ degradation on validation (val_slope=0.0060, only 8.2% of train). This indicates features │
│                          │ are regime-specific - they learn patterns based on absolute levels that don't transfer    │
│                          │ across market regimes.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The best-performing prior program (combined_score=-2.06) already uses some rank-based     │
│                          │ features like `vol_rank_40`, `ret_rank_20`, `ret3_rank_30`, `rsi_14_rank_40`, and         │
│                          │ `hl_range_rank_40`. These percentile rank features are distribution-invariant - they      │
│                          │ capture relative position within a rolling window rather than absolute values.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I will extend this successful pattern by adding percentile rank transformations for the   │
│                          │ most predictive raw features:                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **ret_3_rank_60**: Rank-normalize the 3-period return to make momentum signals         │
│                          │ regime-invariant                                                                          │
│                          │ 2. **efficiency_20_rank_80**: Rank-normalize efficiency to capture relative trend quality │
│                          │ independent of absolute efficiency levels                                                 │
│                          │ 3. **momentum_regime_rank_60**: Rank-normalize the momentum/volatility ratio to make this │
│                          │ interaction stable across regimes                                                         │
│                          │ 4. **rsi_14_rank_60**: Add a longer-window rank of RSI to complement existing rank        │
│                          │ features                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These additions will:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Stay within the 80-feature budget (current program has ~62 features, adding 4 brings us │
│                          │ to ~66)                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Provide regime-invariant versions of key predictive signals                             │
│                          │ - Potentially push slope_ratio from 8.2% toward 15-20% by reducing regime dependency      │
│                          │ - Build on the proven success of rank features in the best prior programs                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that while absolute feature values change meaning across regimes       │
│                          │ (e.g., 2% vol is high in calm markets, low in turbulent ones), the percentile rank within │
│                          │ a rolling window stays interpretable.                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1129                                                                                   │
