│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_invariant_short_windows                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode directly: the model is learning patterns that     │
│                          │ vanish in the latest regime. I am making the feature set more regime-invariant and more   │
│                          │ sensitive to market-character changes by:                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Extending return z-score normalization to 40/60/80 bars, so the model can compare       │
│                          │ short-term moves against slower regime baselines.                                         │
│                          │ - Adding explicit regime-shift features such as `ret_z_20 - ret_z_60`, `ret_z_40 -        │
│                          │ ret_z_80`, and short-vs-long volatility/efficiency/trend deltas.                          │
│                          │ - Replacing some broad, regime-specific indicators with shorter-horizon normalized        │
│                          │ versions that decay faster but should generalize better.                                  │
│                          │ - Removing time-of-day features, which are relatively weak here and help preserve the     │
│                          │ feature budget below 80.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Slightly reducing over-regularization in XGBoost so the model can express a stronger    │
│                          │ slope without becoming too deep or unstable.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The intent is to raise `pred_std_ratio`, recover `val_slope`, and improve `val_r` /       │
│                          │ `val_DA` without regressing train-vs-val gap too much.                                    │
