│ patch_name               │ shorter_regime_invariant_features                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the core failure mode: the model’s signal decays almost completely by   │
│                          │ validation, which strongly suggests the learned patterns are too regime-specific and too  │
│                          │ dependent on longer horizons. I’m shifting the feature set toward short-memory,           │
│                          │ regime-invariant, and regime-change descriptors.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Replace long lookbacks like 60/200 with shorter 5–20 bar windows where possible.        │
│                          │ - Add rolling z-scores for returns, volatility, volume, and price position so the model   │
│                          │ learns relative state rather than absolute levels.                                        │
│                          │ - Add “change in market character” features such as volatility trend, efficiency trend,   │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend, and dispersion trend.                                              │
│                          │ - Keep the feature count comfortably under 80 and maintain only past data.                │
│                          │ - Preserve existing orderbook/funding support, but encode them through shorter-window     │
│                          │ normalization too.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I’m also making a small hyperparameter adjustment to slightly increase model capacity     │
│                          │ while reducing over-regularization. This should help lift prediction variance and slope   │
│                          │ without pushing too hard into overfit.                                                    │
