╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multiscale_regime_shift                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the core failure mode: the model’s slope collapses in the newest regime │
│                          │ because it relies too much on absolute-state features and not enough on regime-invariant, │
│                          │ short-memory signals.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The feature changes add:                                                                  │
│                          │ - longer rolling return z-scores at 40/60/80 bars, which are more stable across           │
│                          │ volatility regimes than raw returns,                                                      │
│                          │ - explicit regime-shift deltas between short and long z-scores, so the model can detect   │
│                          │ when the market character is changing rather than only its current level,                 │
│                          │ - a short-horizon momentum × volatility-regime interaction that is easier to transfer     │
│                          │ across regimes than raw momentum alone.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To keep feature count bounded and reduce low-value periodicity noise, the time-of-day     │
│                          │ features are removed. This makes room for the new regime features while staying           │
│                          │ comfortably under the 80-feature limit.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hyperparameter changes slightly increase expressivity while keeping regularization    │
│                          │ present:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - a bit more depth and trees,                                                             │
│                          │ - lower min_child_weight,                                                                 │
│                          │ - slightly weaker regularization,                                                         │
│                          │ - slightly slower learning with more boosting rounds.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is intended to recover slope without reverting to the very overfit, regime-specific  │
│                          │ behavior seen earlier.                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 4                                                                                         │
