├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ regime_shortlook_xgb                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover version combines the stronger parts of the earlier feature sets with the   │
│                          │ current implementation’s regime-shift focus, while removing the heavy regularization that │
│                          │ caused prediction collapse.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main changes:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Uses shorter lookbacks more aggressively (5–20 bars) and adds rolling z-score           │
│                          │ normalization to make features more regime-invariant.                                     │
│                          │ - Adds explicit regime-change features: volatility trend, autocorrelation trend,          │
│                          │ efficiency trend, dispersion trend.                                                       │
│                          │ - Keeps robust interaction terms, especially momentum × volatility regime and momentum ×  │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Simplifies the feature set to stay well under 80 columns and reduce redundant           │
│                          │ long-horizon signals.                                                                     │
│                          │ - Loosens XGBoost regularization versus the current program to increase predictive slope  │
│                          │ and prediction variance, while still using modest safeguards against overfit.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to recover val slope and prediction dispersion without regressing too far on  │
│                          │ directional accuracy.                                                                     │
