╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ regime_shift_xgb_crossover                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the strongest parts of the prior programs while emphasizing the main │
│                          │ failure mode: regime fragility and prediction collapse. The feature set is rebuilt around │
│                          │ shorter lookbacks, rolling z-scores, and “change in market character” signals such as     │
│                          │ volatility trend, efficiency trend, and regime shifts. I also keep a compact set of       │
│                          │ interactions like momentum × volatility regime, which often generalize better than raw    │
│                          │ signals alone.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the model side, I make XGBoost slightly more expressive than the most over-regularized │
│                          │ versions, while still retaining enough constraint to avoid overfitting. The target        │
│                          │ clipping is loosened a bit to preserve amplitude, and winsorization is applied after      │
│                          │ feature construction to reduce tail dominance without destroying signal.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result is a compact, regime-aware feature crossover designed to improve val slope,    │
│                          │ val correlation, and prediction variance without exceeding the feature budget or using    │
│                          │ any lookahead.                                                                            │
