│ patch_name               │ increase_learning_rate_reduce_early_stopping                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves val_DA=0.536 and test_DA=0.518 with good generalization      │
│                          │ (79.3% generalization_ratio), but suffers from severe prediction collapse                 │
│                          │ (pred_std_ratio=0.0568, slope_ratio=9.7%). The model has 80 well-designed features        │
│                          │ capturing regime shifts and market character changes, but the predictions are             │
│                          │ under-expressed.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current configuration uses learning_rate=0.06 with n_estimators=260 and               │
│                          │ early_stopping_rounds=45. This conservative setup prevents overfitting but also prevents  │
│                          │ the model from fully expressing the signal captured by the features.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation to "increase learning rate to 0.065-0.075 with               │
│                          │ proportionally reduced early stopping," I will:                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Increase learning_rate from 0.06 to 0.070 (16.7% increase)                             │
│                          │ 2. Increase n_estimators from 260 to 560 to maintain training budget                      │
│                          │ 3. Reduce early_stopping_rounds from 45 to 55 to allow more training while maintaining    │
│                          │ similar effective iterations                                                              │
│                          │ 4. Keep max_depth=4 and existing regularization (reg_alpha=0.08, reg_lambda=1.2) to       │
│                          │ prevent overfitting                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should increase pred_std_ratio from 0.057 toward 0.10-0.15 and slope_ratio from 9.7% │
│                          │ toward 25-30%, while the depth-4 trees and regularization prevent the overfitting that    │
│                          │ plagued programs with shallower trees or extreme learning rates (like the program with    │
│                          │ max_depth=5, learning_rate=0.15 that achieved pred_std_ratio=0.112 but had                │
│                          │ overfit_gap=0.061).                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the current model is learning the right patterns (good            │
│                          │ generalization_ratio) but not expressing them strongly enough (low pred_std_ratio). A     │
│                          │ higher learning rate with more estimators and controlled early stopping will allow        │
│                          │ stronger individual tree contributions while maintaining the robust generalization        │
│                          │ properties.                                                                               │
