│ patch_name               │ less_regularization_more_slope                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current model is still over-regularized: train slope is present, but predictions      │
│                          │ collapse sharply toward the mean on val, and pred_std_ratio remains far below target. The │
│                          │ safest next step is to keep the successful depth-4 structure while reducing shrinkage     │
│                          │ from both L1/L2 and the split penalty, and slightly relaxing node constraints so the      │
│                          │ model can express more persistent signal across the train→test→val regime shifts.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ - lowers `reg_alpha` and `reg_lambda` to reduce prediction collapse,                      │
│                          │ - lowers `min_child_weight` and `gamma` slightly to allow more useful splits,             │
│                          │ - keeps the architecture conservative (`max_depth=4`) to avoid regressing into unstable   │
│                          │ overfit,                                                                                  │
│                          │ - trims `early_stopping_rounds` a bit so the larger model does not over-train.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ No feature changes are needed here because the current feature set already improved       │
│                          │ generalization ratio substantially; the bottleneck is now underfitting / collapsed        │
